! A nickel chain with an iodine beside each bond, as a spin spiral along the chain
! on fully-relativistic datasets with the coupling switched off (soc_scale = 0).
! The zeroth order of P123: the spin-orbit coupling is added to first order on
! it by spiral_spin_orbit_energy, and the first-order energy is n . V(q).
!
! Nickel 4.4 bohr apart along z, the iodine 4.4 bohr off the chain along x at the
! bond midpoint (Ni-I 4.92 bohr), 13 x 12 bohr of box. The iodine breaks inversion
! and leaves one mirror, the plane of the atoms (y -> -y), so V can only point
! along y: the coupling tells a cycloid turning in the plane of the atoms from its
! mirror image, and a helix (axis along the chain) or a cycloid across the plane
! (axis along x) gets nothing at first order. Iodine carries the strong 5p
! coupling, the Fert-Levy mechanism of NiI2.
!
! Deliberately small (34 Ry) so that the spiral, its -q partner and the four-cell
! supercell of nii-chain-4cell.in run in a test. The cutoff is chosen so that the
! supercell's FFT grid is this one's repeated exactly (18 and 72 along the chain):
! at 30 Ry it is 15 and 64, the exchange-correlation potential is then evaluated on
! other points, and the supercell's first-order energy moved 1.3 per cent. The k-points carry contributions to
! V a hundred times larger than their sum, so V is far from converged in k here;
! the tests are identities at this sampling and do not depend on that. Eight
! k-points rather than four: at four the SCF limit-cycles near 1.7e-8 Ry. The
! 1 1 8 grid folds onto the supercell's 1 1 2: k + q/2 = (j + 1)/8 b3, which is 0 or
! half a supercell reciprocal vector. conv_thr = 1e-9 because 1e-10 takes over a
! hundred iterations here (1.77e-10 at 100, crawling); the identities are taken at
! one fixed density and do not depend on it, and the one test that compares two
! SCFs states the floor it measured at this threshold.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 8, celldm(1) = 13.0, celldm(2) = 0.92307692307692, celldm(3) = 0.33846153846154,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 2, ecutwfc = 34.0, nbnd = 34,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'mv', degauss = 0.03, nosym = .true.,
    noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true., soc_scale = 0.0,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5, angle1(1) = 90.0,
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.0,
    spiral_q(1) = 0.0, spiral_q(2) = 0.0, spiral_q(3) = 0.25
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-9, mixing_beta = 0.3
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Ni 58.69 Ni.rel-pbe-nc-dojo.UPF
 I 126.90 I.rel-pbe-nc-dojo.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS bohr
 Ni 4.3 6.0 0.0
 I  8.7 6.0 2.2
K_POINTS (automatic)
 1 1 8 0 0 0
